    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **264 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` feature following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern used in the codebase.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `capacityWarning` boolean field to the Owner schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), documenting it as true when the city holds 40\u201349 owners.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct doesn't try to map it from the entity (it's a derived, controller-computed value, exactly like `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant and an `isApproachingCapacity(city)` helper that returns true when `countOwnersInCity(city)` is in `[40, 49]` (i.e. `>= 40 && < MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`), reusing the existing count logic.\n   - Set `ownerDto.setCapacityWarning(...)` in the three response paths where `bulkSignupWarning` is set: `getOwner`, the idempotent-replay branch of `addOwner`, and the main create path.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`countOwnersInCity(...) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` \u2192 409) is untouched \u2014 and because a full city can't be created past 50, the warning window naturally caps at 49.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes, as do the existing capacity rejection/allow tests and the entire suite.",
